"startAngle","description":"<p>Specifies the start angle for the series in a polar or radar chart, measured in degrees from the horizontal axis, determining the initial angle from which the series begins.</p>\n","type":"number","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#startangle"},"isInversed":{"name":"isInversed","description":"<p>If set to true, the axis will be rendered in an inversed manner.</p>\n","type":"boolean","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#isinversed"},"line":{"name":"line","description":"<p>Sets and gets the options for customizing the appearance of the axis line.</p>\n","type":"LineModel","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/linear-gauge/axis#line"},"opposedPosition":{"name":"opposedPosition","description":"<p>If set to true, the axis will render on the opposite side of its default position.</p>\n","type":"boolean","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#opposedposition"},"border":{"name":"border","description":"<p>Configures the appearance of the border around multi-level labels, including the color, width, and type of the border.</p>\n","type":"LabelBorderModel","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#border"},"enableTrim":{"name":"enableTrim","description":"<p>If set to true, axis labels will be trimmed based on the <code>maximumLabelWidth</code>.</p>\n","type":"boolean","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#enabletrim"},"increment":{"name":"increment","description":"<p>Specifies the increment for an axis label. When this property is set, the displayed text of the labels will be multiplied with the increment value.</p>\n","type":"number","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/heatmap/axis#increment"},"interval":{"name":"interval","description":"<p>Specifies the interval for the axis.</p>\n","type":"number","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#interval"},"intervalType":{"name":"intervalType","description":"<p>The <code>intervalType</code> property defines how the intervals on a date-time axis are calculated and displayed.\nAvailable options are:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Auto: Automatically determines the interval type based on the data and chart settings.</li>\n<li>Years: Sets the interval of the axis in years.</li>\n<li>Months: Sets the interval of the axis in months.</li>\n<li>Days: Sets the interval of the axis in days.</li>\n<li>Hours: Sets the interval of the axis in hours.</li>\n<li>Minutes: Sets the interval of the axis in minutes.</li>\n</ul>\n","type":"string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#intervaltype"},"labelFormat":{"name":"labelFormat","description":"<p>Used to format the axis label. This property accepts global string formats such as <code>C</code>, <code>n1</code>, <code>P</code>, etc.\nIt also accepts placeholders like <code>{value}°C</code>, where <code>{value}</code> represents the axis label (e.g., 20°C).</p>\n","type":"string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#labelformat"},"labelIntersectAction":{"name":"labelIntersectAction","description":"<p>Specifies the action to take when axis labels intersect with each other.\nThe available options are:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>None: Shows all labels without any modification.</li>\n<li>Hide: Hides the label if it intersects with another label.</li>\n<li>Trim: Trims the label text to fit within the available space.</li>\n<li>Wrap: Wraps the label text to fit within the available space.</li>\n<li>MultipleRows: Displays the label text in multiple rows to avoid intersection.</li>\n<li>Rotate45: Rotates the label text by 45 degrees to avoid intersection.</li>\n<li>Rotate90: Rotates the label text by 90 degrees to avoid intersection.</li>\n</ul>\n","type":"string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#labelintersectaction"},"labelRotation":{"name":"labelRotation","description":"<p>The angle to which the axis label gets rotated.</p>\n","type":"number","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#labelrotation"},"labels":{"name":"labels","description":"<p>Sets and gets the list of texts to be displayed in an axis as labels.</p>\n","type":"string[]","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/heatmap/axis#labels"},"maxLabelLength":{"name":"maxLabelLength","description":"<p>Specifies the maximum length of the axis labels.</p>\n","type":"number","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/heatmap/axis#maxlabellength"},"multiLevelLabels":{"name":"multiLevelLabels","description":"<p>Multi-level labels are used to display hierarchical or grouped labels on the axis, allowing for a more detailed and structured data representation.</p>\n","type":"MultiLevelLabelsModel[]","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#multilevellabels"},"multiLevelSize":{"name":"multiLevelSize","description":"","type":"Size[]","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/heatmap/axis#multilevelsize"},"showLabelOn":{"name":"showLabelOn","description":"<p>Specifies the axis label display type for the date time axis. The following are available types,</p>\n<ul>\n<li>None: Axis labels displayed based on the value type.</li>\n<li>Years: Displays the axis labels for every year.</li>\n<li>Months: Displays the axis labels for every month.</li>\n<li>Days: Displays the axis labels for every day.</li>\n<li>Hours: Displays the axis labels for every hour.</li>\n</ul>\n","type":"string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/heatmap/axis#showlabelon"},"textStyle":{"name":"textStyle","description":"<p>Sets and gets the options to customize the axis labels.</p>\n","type":"FontModel","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/heatmap/axis#textstyle"},"title":{"name":"title","description":"<p>Specifies the title of an axis, displayed along the axis to provide context about the represented data.</p>\n","type":"string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#title"},"valueType":{"name":"valueType","description":"<p>The <code>valueType</code> property defines the type of data that the axis can manage, ensuring correct rendering based on the data type. This property supports multiple data types, each suited for different kinds of data visualization.\nAvailable options include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Double: Used for rendering a numeric axis to accommodate numeric data.</li>\n<li>DateTime: Utilized for rendering a date-time axis to manage date-time data.</li>\n<li>Category: Employed for rendering a category axis to manage categorical data.</li>\n<li>Logarithmic: Applied for rendering a logarithmic axis to handle a wide range of values.</li>\n<li>DateTimeCategory: Used to render a date-time category axis for managing business days.</li>\n</ul>\n","type":"string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#valuetype"},"majorGridLines":{"name":"majorGridLines","description":"<p>Options for customizing major grid lines on the axis.</p>\n","type":"MajorGridLinesModel","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#majorgridlines"},"minorGridLines":{"name":"minorGridLines","description":"<p>Options for customizing minor grid lines on the axis.</p>\n","type":"MinorGridLinesModel","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#minorgridlines"},"visible":{"name":"visible","description":"<p>If set to true, axis labels will be visible in the chart. By default, axis labels are enabled.</p>\n","type":"boolean","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#visible"},"coefficient":{"name":"coefficient","description":"<p>The <code>coefficient</code> value adjusts the size of the polar radar chart's radius. A higher value increases the radius size, while a smaller value decreases it.</p>\n","type":"number","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#coefficient"},"columnIndex":{"name":"columnIndex","description":"<p>Specifies the index of the column where the axis is associated when the chart area is divided into multiple plot areas using <code>columns</code>.</p>\n","type":"number","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#columnindex"},"crossesAt":{"name":"crossesAt","description":"<p>Specifies the value at which the axis line intersects with the vertical axis or vice versa.</p>\n","type":"Object","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#crossesat"},"crossesInAxis":{"name":"crossesInAxis","description":"<p>Specifies the name of the axis with which the axis line should intersect.</p>\n","type":"string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#crossesinaxis"},"crosshairTooltip":{"name":"crosshairTooltip","description":"<p>Options to customize the appearance and behavior of the crosshair tooltip that appears when hovering over the chart.</p>\n","type":"CrosshairTooltipModel","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#crosshairtooltip"},"description":{"name":"description","description":"<p>A description for the axis that provides additional information about its content for screen readers.</p>\n","type":"string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#description"},"desiredIntervals":{"name":"desiredIntervals","description":"<p>The <code>desiredIntervals</code> property allows the axis to calculate intervals that are roughly equal to the specified number, promoting a more readable and evenly spaced axis.</p>\n","type":"number","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#desiredintervals"},"edgeLabelPlacement":{"name":"edgeLabelPlacement","description":"<p>The <code>edgeLabelPlacement</code> property ensures that labels positioned at the edges of the axis do not overlap with the axis boundaries or other chart elements, offering several options to improve chart readability by managing edge labels effectively.\nAvailable options are:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>None: No action will be performed on edge labels.</li>\n<li>Hide: Edge labels will be hidden to prevent overlap.</li>\n<li>Shift: Edge labels will be shifted to fit within the axis bounds without overlapping.</li>\n</ul>\n","type":"string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#edgelabelplacement"},"enableAutoIntervalOnZooming":{"name":"enableAutoIntervalOnZooming","description":"<p>If set to true, the axis interval will be calculated automatically based on the zoomed range.</p>\n","type":"boolean","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#enableautointervalonzooming"},"enableScrollbarOnZooming":{"name":"enableScrollbarOnZooming","description":"<p>If set to true, a scrollbar will appear while zooming to help navigate through the zoomed content.</p>\n","type":"boolean","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#enablescrollbaronzooming"},"enableWrap":{"name":"enableWrap","description":"<p>Specifies whether the axis labels should be wrapped based on the specified <code>maximumLabelWidth</code>.\nWhen set to <code>true</code>, the axis labels will automatically wrap to fit within the available width defined by <code>maximumLabelWidth</code>.</p>\n","type":"boolean","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#enablewrap"},"isIndexed":{"name":"isIndexed","description":"<p>If set to true, data points are rendered based on their index.</p>\n","type":"boolean","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#isindexed"},"labelPadding":{"name":"labelPadding","description":"<p>The <code>labelPadding</code> property adjusts the distance to ensure a clear space between the axis labels and the axis line.</p>\n","type":"number","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#labelpadding"},"labelPlacement":{"name":"labelPlacement","description":"<p>The <code>labelPlacement</code> property controls where the category axis labels are rendered in relation to the axis ticks.\nAvailable options are:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>BetweenTicks: Renders the label between the axis ticks.</li>\n<li>OnTicks: Renders the label directly on the axis ticks.</li>\n</ul>\n","type":"string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#labelplacement"},"labelPosition":{"name":"labelPosition","description":"<p>The <code>labelPosition</code> property determines where the axis labels are rendered in relation to the axis line.\nAvailable options are:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Inside: Renders the labels inside the axis line.</li>\n<li>Outside: Renders the labels outside the axis line.</li>\n</ul>\n","type":"string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#labelposition"},"labelTemplate":{"name":"labelTemplate","description":"<p>Specifies the template used to render axis labels, allowing for customized labels with text, images, or other UI elements.\nThe template is provided as a string with placeholders for interpolation. Use <code>${label}</code> to insert the axis label and <code>${value}</code> for the axis label value.\nFor security, string templates use dangerouslySetInnerHTML in React—ensure input is trusted to avoid XSS vulnerabilities.\nIf null or undefined, the axis will render default labels.\nCompatible with both categorical and numerical axes.</p>\n","type":"string|Function","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#labeltemplate"},"lineBreakAlignment":{"name":"lineBreakAlignment","description":"<p>Determines the alignment of labels when a line break occurs in the axis labels.</p>\n","type":"string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#linebreakalignment"},"logBase":{"name":"logBase","description":"<p>Specifies the base value for a logarithmic axis.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Note that <code>valueType</code> must be set to <code>Logarithmic</code> for this feature to work.</p>\n</blockquote>\n","type":"number","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#logbase"},"majorTickLines":{"name":"majorTickLines","description":"<p>Options for customizing major tick lines on the axis.</p>\n","type":"MajorTickLinesModel","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#majorticklines"},"maximumLabelWidth":{"name":"maximumLabelWidth","description":"<p>Specifies the maximum width of an axis label.</p>\n","type":"number","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#maximumlabelwidth"},"maximumLabels":{"name":"maximumLabels","description":"<p>Specifies the maximum number of labels per 100 pixels relative to the axis length.</p>\n","type":"number","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#maximumlabels"},"minorTickLines":{"name":"minorTickLines","description":"<p>Options for customizing minor tick lines on the axis.</p>\n","type":"MinorTickLinesModel","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#minorticklines"},"minorTicksPerInterval":{"name":"minorTicksPerInterval","description":"<p>Specifies the number of minor ticks per interval.</p>\n","type":"number","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#minorticksperinterval"},"name":{"name":"name","description":"<p>A unique identifier for an axis. To associate an axis with a series, set this name to the <code>xAxisName</code> or <code>yAxisName</code> properties of the series.</p>\n","type":"string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#name"},"placeNextToAxisLine":{"name":"placeNextToAxisLine","description":"<p>Specifies whether axis elements, such as axis labels and the axis title, should be crossed by the axis line.</p>\n","type":"boolean","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#placenexttoaxisline"},"plotOffset":{"name":"plotOffset","description":"<p>Specifies the padding on the top, bottom, left and right sides of the chart area, in pixels.</p>\n","type":"number","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#plotoffset"},"plotOffsetBottom":{"name":"plotOffsetBottom","description":"<p>Specifies the bottom padding for the chart area, in pixels.</p>\n","type":"number","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#plotoffsetbottom"},"plotOffsetLeft":{"name":"plotOffsetLeft","description":"<p>Specifies the left padding for the chart area, in pixels.</p>\n","type":"number","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#plotoffsetleft"},"plotOffsetRight":{"name":"plotOffsetRight","description":"<p>Specifies the right padding for the chart area, in pixels.</p>\n","type":"number","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#plotoffsetright"},"plotOffsetTop":{"name":"plotOffsetTop","description":"<p>Specifies the top padding for the chart area, in pixels.</p>\n","type":"number","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#plotoffsettop"},"rangePadding":{"name":"rangePadding","description":"<p>The <code>rangePadding</code> property determines how padding is applied to the axis range, affecting the appearance of the chart by adjusting the minimum and maximum values of the axis.\nAvailable options are:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>None: No padding is applied to the axis.</li>\n<li>Normal: Padding is applied based on the range calculation.</li>\n<li>Additional: The interval of the axis is added as padding to both the minimum and maximum values of the range.</li>\n<li>Round: The axis range is rounded to the nearest possible value that is divisible by the interval.</li>\n</ul>\n","type":"string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#rangepadding"},"rowIndex":{"name":"rowIndex","description":"<p>Specifies the index of the row where the axis is associated when the chart area is divided into multiple plot areas using <code>rows</code>.</p>\n","type":"number","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#rowindex"},"scrollbarSettings":{"name":"scrollbarSettings","description":"<p>Configures the scrollbar with options for customization, including appearance, behavior, and lazy loading settings.</p>\n","type":"ScrollbarSettingsModel","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#scrollbarsettings"},"skeleton":{"name":"skeleton","description":"<p>Specifies the skeleton format used for processing date-time values.</p>\n","type":"string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#skeleton"},"skeletonType":{"name":"skeletonType","description":"<p>Specifies the format type to be used in date-time formatting.</p>\n","type":"string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#skeletontype"},"span":{"name":"span","description":"<p>Specifies the number of <code>columns</code> or <code>rows</code> that an axis spans horizontally or vertically.</p>\n","type":"number","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#span"},"startFromZero":{"name":"startFromZero","description":"<p>If set to true, the axis starts from zero.\nIf set to false, the axis starts from the minimum value of the data.</p>\n","type":"boolean","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#startfromzero"},"stripLines":{"name":"stripLines","description":"<p>Specifies the collection of strip lines for the axis, which are visual elements used to mark or highlight specific ranges.</p>\n","type":"StripLineSettingsModel[]","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#striplines"},"tabIndex":{"name":"tabIndex","description":"<p>The <code>tabIndex</code> value for the axis, determining its position in the tab order.</p>\n","type":"number","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#tabindex"},"tickPosition":{"name":"tickPosition","description":"<p>The <code>tickPosition</code> property determines where the axis ticks are rendered in relation to the axis line.\nAvailable options are:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Inside: Renders the ticks inside the axis line.</li>\n<li>Outside: Renders the ticks outside the axis line.</li>\n</ul>\n","type":"string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#tickposition"},"titlePadding":{"name":"titlePadding","description":"<p>Specifies the padding between the axis title and the axis labels.</p>\n","type":"number","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#titlepadding"},"titleRotation":{"name":"titleRotation","description":"<p>Defines an angle for rotating the axis title. By default, the angle is calculated based on the position and orientation of the axis.</p>\n","type":"number","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#titlerotation"},"titleStyle":{"name":"titleStyle","description":"<p>Options for customizing the appearance of the axis title, including font family, size, style, weight, and color.</p>\n","type":"FontModel","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#titlestyle"},"zoomFactor":{"name":"zoomFactor","description":"<p>The axis is scaled by this factor. When <code>zoomFactor</code> is 0.5, the chart is scaled by 200% along this axis.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Note the value ranges from 0 to 1.</p>\n</blockquote>\n","type":"number","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#zoomfactor"},"zoomPosition":{"name":"zoomPosition","description":"<p>Sets the position of the zoomed axis on the chart, with the <code>zoomPosition</code> property specifying the position within the zoomed range, from 0 (start) to 1 (end).</p>\n","type":"number","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/axis#zoomposition"},"zoomingScrollBar":{"name":"zoomingScrollBar","description":"","typ