rticular selected cell is deselected from the pivot table.</p>\n","type":"Event","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/pivotview/gridSettings#celldeselected"},"cellDeselecting":{"name":"cellDeselecting","description":"<p>It triggers before the selected cell is deselecting from the pivot table.</p>\n","type":"Event","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/pivotview/gridSettings#celldeselecting"},"cellSelected":{"name":"cellSelected","description":"<p>It triggers after a cell is selected in the pivot table.\\</p>\n","type":"Event","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/pivotview/gridSettings#cellselected"},"cellSelecting":{"name":"cellSelecting","description":"<p>It triggers before any cell selection occurs in the pivot table.</p>\n","type":"Event","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/pivotview/gridSettings#cellselecting"},"columnDrag":{"name":"columnDrag","description":"<p>It triggers when column header element is dragged (moved) continuously.</p>\n","type":"Event","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/pivotview/gridSettings#columndrag"},"columnDragStart":{"name":"columnDragStart","description":"<p>It triggers when column header element drag (move) starts.</p>\n","type":"Event","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/pivotview/gridSettings#columndragstart"},"columnDrop":{"name":"columnDrop","description":"<p>It triggers when a column header element is dropped on the target column.</p>\n","type":"Event","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/pivotview/gridSettings#columndrop"},"columnRender":{"name":"columnRender","description":"<p>It allows to configure the column before it renders.</p>\n","type":"Event","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/pivotview/gridSettings#columnrender"},"contextMenuClick":{"name":"contextMenuClick","description":"<p>It triggers when click on context menu.</p>\n","type":"Event","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/pivotview/gridSettings#contextmenuclick"},"contextMenuOpen":{"name":"contextMenuOpen","description":"<p>It triggers before context menu opens.</p>\n","type":"Event","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/pivotview/gridSettings#contextmenuopen"},"excelHeaderQueryCellInfo":{"name":"excelHeaderQueryCellInfo","description":"<p>It triggers before exporting each header cell to Excel file.\nYou can also customize the Excel cells.</p>\n","type":"Event","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/pivotview/gridSettings#excelheaderquerycellinfo"},"excelQueryCellInfo":{"name":"excelQueryCellInfo","description":"<p>It triggers before exporting each cell to Excel file.\nYou can also customize the Excel cells.</p>\n","type":"Event","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/pivotview/gridSettings#excelquerycellinfo"},"headerCellInfo":{"name":"headerCellInfo","description":"<p>Triggered for column header.\nIt will get triggered before the cell element is appended to the Grid element.</p>\n","type":"Event","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/pivotview/gridSettings#headercellinfo"},"pdfHeaderQueryCellInfo":{"name":"pdfHeaderQueryCellInfo","description":"<p>It triggers before exporting each header cell to PDF document. You can also customize the PDF cells.</p>\n","type":"Event","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/pivotview/gridSettings#pdfheaderquerycellinfo"},"pdfQueryCellInfo":{"name":"pdfQueryCellInfo","description":"<p>It triggers before exporting each cell to PDF document. You can also customize the PDF cells.</p>\n","type":"Event","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/pivotview/gridSettings#pdfquerycellinfo"},"printComplete":{"name":"printComplete","description":"<p>It triggers after print action is completed.</p>\n","type":"Event","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/pivotview/gridSettings#printcomplete"},"queryCellInfo":{"name":"queryCellInfo","description":"<p>Triggered every time a request is made to access cell information, element, or data.\nIt will get triggered before the cell element is appended to the Grid element.</p>\n","type":"Event","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/pivotview/gridSettings#querycellinfo"},"rowDeselected":{"name":"rowDeselected","description":"<p>It triggers when a selected row is deselected from the pivot table.</p>\n","type":"Event","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/pivotview/gridSettings#rowdeselected"},"rowDeselecting":{"name":"rowDeselecting","description":"<p>It triggers before deselecting the selected row from the pivot table.</p>\n","type":"Event","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/pivotview/gridSettings#rowdeselecting"},"rowSelected":{"name":"rowSelected","description":"<p>It triggers after a row is selected in the pivot table.</p>\n","type":"Event","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/pivotview/gridSettings#rowselected"},"rowSelecting":{"name":"rowSelecting","description":"<p>It triggers before row selection occurs in the pivot table.</p>\n","type":"Event","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/pivotview/gridSettings#rowselecting"},"allowAutoResizing":{"name":"allowAutoResizing","description":"<p>Allows the component to be fit based on the width of its columns.</p>\n","type":"boolean","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/pivotview/gridSettings#allowautoresizing"},"allowReordering":{"name":"allowReordering","description":"<p>Allows to reorder a specific column header from one index to another index in the pivot table by drag-and-drop.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Reordering allows only at the same level as the column headers in the pivot table.</p>\n</blockquote>\n","type":"boolean","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/pivotview/gridSettings#allowreordering"},"allowSelection":{"name":"allowSelection","description":"<p>Allows a row or column or cell to be highlighted by simply clicking or arrow key in the pivot table.</p>\n","type":"boolean","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/pivotview/gridSettings#allowselection"},"clipMode":{"name":"clipMode","description":"<p>Allows the contents of the cell overflow to be displayed in the pivot table.\nFor example, to truncate the cell content of a cell when it overflows with respect to its cell width, set the property <code>clipMode</code> to <strong>Clip</strong>.\nThe modes available are:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>Clip</code>: Allow the content of a cell to truncate when it overflows its content area.</li>\n<li><code>Ellipsis</code>: Allows the content of a cell to be displayed as an ellipse when it overflows its content area.</li>\n<li><code>EllipsisWithTooltip</code>: Allows the cell content to be displayed as an ellipse when its content area is overflowing.\nAnd the tooltip will also be displayed while hovering on the ellipsis applied cell.</li>\n</ul>\n","type":"ClipMode","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/pivotview/gridSettings#clipmode"},"columnWidth":{"name":"columnWidth","description":"<p>Allow to set width to the pivot table columns commonly.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>By default, the columnWidth property is set as 110 pixels to each column except the first column.\nThe first column always defined as row headers in the pivot table. For first column,\n250 pixels and 200 pixels are set respectively with and without grouping bar.</p>\n</blockquote>\n","type":"number","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/pivotview/gridSettings#columnwidth"},"contextMenuItems":{"name":"contextMenuItems","description":"<p>Allows to show built-in context with pre-defined menu option or custom menu options by simply right clicking on the pivot table cell.\nThe options available are:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>Drillthrough</code>: Allows to show the drill-through dialog over the pivot table to perform drill-through operations.</li>\n<li><code>Expand</code>: Allows to expand the collapsed row or column headers in the pivot table.</li>\n<li><code>Collapse</code>: Allows to collapse the expanded row or column headers in the pivot table.</li>\n<li><code>CalculatedField</code>: Allows to show the calculated field dialog over the pivot table to perform calculated field operations.</li>\n<li><code>Pdf Export</code>: Allows to export the pivot table as PDF format.</li>\n<li><code>Excel Export</code>: Allows to export the pivot table as Excel format.</li>\n<li><code>Csv Export</code>: Allows to export the pivot table as CSV format.</li>\n<li><code>Sort Ascending</code>: Allows to perform ascending order with respect to the values on selected cell contained row or column in the pivot table.</li>\n<li><code>Sort Descending</code>: Allows to perform descending order with respect to the values on selected cell contained row or column in the pivot table.</li>\n<li><code>Aggregate</code>: Allow options to perform calculations over a group of values (exclusively for value fields bound in value axis) using the aggregation option in the pivot table.</li>\n</ul>\n","type":"PivotTableContextMenuItem[]|ContextMenuItemModel[]","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/pivotview/gridSettings#contextmenuitems"},"height":{"name":"height","description":"<p>Allow the height of the pivot table content to be set, meaning that the height given should be applied without considering the column headers in the pivot table.</p>\n","type":"number|string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/pivotview/gridSettings#height"},"layout":{"name":"layout","description":"<p>Specifies the layout options for displaying the pivot table in either a compact or tabular format.\nThe available options are:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>Compact</code>: Displays the pivot table in a compact format, merging row headers into a single column.</li>\n<li><code>Tabular</code>: Displays the pivot table in a traditional format with separate columns for row headers, creating a more detailed table format.</li>\n</ul>\n","type":"string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/pivotview/gridSettings#layout"},"printMode":{"name":"printMode","description":"<p>Allow options to print either the current page shown in the pivot table on its own or the entire pivot table.\nThe options available are:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>AllPages</code>: Prints the entire pivot table.</li>\n<li><code>CurrentPage</code>: Prints the current page shown in the pivot table on its own.</li>\n</ul>\n","type":"PrintMode","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/pivotview/gridSettings#printmode"},"repeatItemLabels":{"name":"repeatItemLabels","description":"<p>Allows the item and field labels to be repeated in the pivot table.\nWhen set to <code>true</code>, the item and field labels will be repeated for each hierarchical level\nwithin a field, making every row and column header consistently visible when expanded.\nThis mimics the &quot;Repeat Item Labels&quot; feature in Microsoft Excel.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>This property is applicable only for tabular layout with relational data source.</p>\n</blockquote>\n","type":"boolean","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/pivotview/gridSettings#repeatitemlabels"},"selectedRowIndex":{"name":"selectedRowIndex","description":"<p>Allows to highlight specific row in the pivot table during initial rendering.\nFor example, to highlight the pivot table's first row, set the property <code>selectedRowIndex</code> to <strong>0</strong>.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>You can get the currently selected row index of the pivot table from the <code>selectedRowIndex</code> property using pivot table instance at run-time.</p>\n</blockquote>\n","type":"number","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/pivotview/gridSettings#selectedrowindex"},"selectionSettings":{"name":"selectionSettings","description":"<p>Allows set of options to customize the selection of a row or column or cell by simply clicking on the arrow key in the pivot table.\nThe options available are:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>mode - Allow options to highlight either row wise or column wise or specific cells in the pivot table. For example, to highlight the columns, set the property </code>mode` to <strong>Column</strong>.</li>\n<li><code>cellSelectionMode</code>: Allow options to customize the mode of selection to highlight either row wise or column wise or specific cell in the pivot table.\nFor example, to apply the selection that includes in between cells of rows within the range, set the property <code>cellSelectionMode</code> to <strong>Box</strong>.</li>\n<li><code>type</code>: Allow options to customize the selection type to highlight either row wise or column wise or specific cell in the pivot table.\nFor example, to highlight multiple rows or columns or cells, set the property <code>type</code> to <strong>Multiple</strong>.</li>\n<li><code>checkboxOnly</code>: Allows the selection options to highlight the rows in the pivot table using checkbox selection on their own.</li>\n<li><code>persistSelection</code>: Allows you to keep selections in rows or columns or cells while performing all operations in the pivot table.</li>\n<li><code>checkboxMode</code>: Allow options to customize the checkbox selection mode in the pivot table.\nFor example, to select multiple rows one by one through simple clicking on rows, set the property <code>checkboxMode</code> to <strong>Default</strong>.</li>\n<li><code>enableSimpleMultiRowSelection</code>: Allows to perform multiple selection in rows with single clicks without using <strong>SHIFT</strong> or <strong>CTRL</strong> keys.</li>\n</ul>\n","type":"SelectionSettingsModel|SelectionSettings","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/pivotview/gridSettings#selectionsettings"},"textWrapSettings":{"name":"textWrapSettings","description":"<p>Allows the options for customizing the content of the cells to be wrapped in either rows and column headers or values or both headers and values in the pivot table.\nFor example, to wrap the contents of the value cells in the pivot table, then set the property <code>wrapMode</code> to <strong>Content</strong> in the <code>textWrapSettings</code> class.\nThe options available are:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>Both</code>: Allows the content of the cells to be wrapped in both headers and values.</li>\n<li><code>Header</code>: Allows the content of the cells to be wrapped in rows and column headers alone.</li>\n<li><code>Content</code>: Allows the content of the cells to be packed for the value cells alone.</li>\n</ul>\n","type":"TextWrapSettings","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/pivotview/gridSettings#textwrapsettings"},"width":{"name":"width","description":"<p>Allow to set width of the pivot table.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The pivot table will not display less than 400px, as it is the minimum width to the component.</p>\n</blockquote>\n","type":"number|string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/pivotview/gridSettings#width"}},"MultiColumnComboBox":{"actionBegin":{"name":"actionBegin","description":"<p>Triggers before fetching data from the remote server.</p>\n","type":"Event","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/multicolumn-combobox/#actionbegin"},"actionComplete":{"name":"actionComplete","description":"<p>Triggers after data is fetched successfully from the remote server.</p>\n","type":"Event","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/multicolumn-combobox/#actioncomplete"},"actionFailure":{"name":"actionFailure","description":"<p>Triggers when the data fetch request from the remote server fails.</p>\n","type":"Event","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/multicolumn-combobox/#actionfailure"},"change":{"name":"change","description":"<p>Triggers when an item in a popup is selected or when the model value is changed by the user.</p>\n","type":"Event","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/multicolumn-combobox/#change"},"close":{"name":"close","description":"<p>Triggers when the popup is closed.</p>\n","type":"Event","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/multicolumn-combobox/#close"},"created":{"name":"created","description":"<p>Event callback that is raised after rendering the control.</p>\n","type":"Event","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/multicolumn-combobox/#created"},"filtering":{"name":"filtering","description":"<p>Triggers on typing a character in the component.</p>\n","type":"Event","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/multicolumn-combobox/#filtering"},"open":{"name":"open","description":"<p>Triggers when the popup opens.</p>\n","type":"Event","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/multicolumn-combobox/#open"},"select":{"name":"select","description":"<p>Triggers when an item in the popup is selected by the user either with mouse/tap or with keyboard navigation.</p>\n","type":"Event","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/multicolumn-combobox/#select"},"actionFailureTemplate":{"name":"actionFailureTemplate","description":"<p>Accepts the template and assigns it to the popup content when the data fetch request from the remote server fails.</p>\n","type":"string|Function","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/multicolumn-combobox/#actionfailuretemplate"},"allowFiltering":{"name":"allowFiltering","description":"<p>Specifies the filter action retrieves matched items through the filtering event based on the characters typed in the search TextBox.\nIf no match is found, the value of the noRecordsTemplate property will be displayed.</p>\n","type":"boolean","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/multicolumn-combobox/#allowfiltering"},"allowServerDataBinding":{"name":"allowServerDataBinding","description":"","type":"boolean","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/multicolumn-combobox/#allowserverdatabinding"},"allowSorting":{"name":"allowSorting","description":"<p>Specifies whether sorting is allowed for the columns in the dropdown list.</p>\n","type":"boolean","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/multicolumn-combobox/#allowsorting"},"columns":{"name":"columns","description":"<p>Specifies the number of columns and its respective fields to be displayed in the dropdown popup.</p>\n","type":"ColumnModel[]","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/multicolumn-combobox/#columns"},"cssClass":{"name":"cssClass","description":"<p>Sets CSS classes to the root element of the component that allows customization of appearance.</p>\n","type":"string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/multicolumn-combobox/#cssclass"},"currentContext":{"name":"currentContext","description":"","type":"Object","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/multicolumn-combobox/#currentcontext"},"dataSource":{"name":"dataSource","description":"<p>Accepts the list items either through local or remote service and binds it to the component.\nIt can be an array of JSON Objects or an instance of <code>DataManager</code>.</p>\n","type":"Object|DataManager|DataResult","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/multicolumn-combobox/#datasource"},"disabled":{"name":"disabled","description":"<p>Specifies a value that indicates whether the component is disabled or not.</p>\n","type":"boolean","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/multicolumn-combobox/#disabled"},"ej2StatePersistenceVersion":{"name":"ej2StatePersistenceVersion","description":"","type":"string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/multicolumn-combobox/#ej2statepersistenceversion"},"element":{"name":"element","description":"","type":"HTMLElement","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/multicolumn-combobox/#element"},"enablePersistence":{"name":"enablePersistence","description":"<p>Specifies the component’s state between page reloads. If enabled, the list of states for the value will be persisted.</p>\n","type":"boolean","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/multicolumn-combobox/#enablepersistence"},"enableRtl":{"name":"enableRtl","description":"<p>Enable or disable rendering component in right to left direction.</p>\n","type":"boolean","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/multicolumn-combobox/#enablertl"},"enableVirtualization":{"name":"enableVirtualization","description":"<p>Defines whether to enable virtual scrolling in the component.</p>\n","type":"boolean","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/multicolumn-combobox/#enablevirtualization"},"fields":{"name":"fields","description":"<p>The <code>fields</code> property maps the columns of the data table and binds the data to the component.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>text - Maps the text column from data table for each list item.</li>\n<li>value - Maps the value column from data table for each list item.</li>\n<li>groupBy - Group the list items with it's related items by mapping groupBy field.</li>\n</ul>\n","type":"FieldSettingsModel","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/multicolumn-combobox/#fields"},"filterType":{"name":"filterType","description":"<p>Determines on which filter type, the component needs to be considered on search action.\nThe <code>FilterType</code> and its supported data types are\n&lt;table&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;\n&lt;td colSpan=1 rowSpan=1&gt;\nFilterType&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colSpan=1 rowSpan=1&gt;\nDescription&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colSpan=1 rowSpan=1&gt;\nSupported Types&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;\n&lt;td colSpan=1 rowSpan=1&gt;\nStartsWith&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colSpan=1 rowSpan=1&gt;\nChecks whether a value begins with the specified value.