]","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/heatmap/series#rectpositioncollection"},"accessibility":{"name":"accessibility","description":"<p>Options to improve accessibility for series elements.</p>\n","type":"SeriesAccessibilityModel","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#accessibility"},"animation":{"name":"animation","description":"<p>Options for customizing the animation of the series.\nBy default, animation is enabled with a duration of 1000 milliseconds (about 1 second). It can be disabled by setting enable to <code>false</code>.\nThe following properties are supported in animation:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>enable: If set to true, the series is animated on initial loading.</li>\n<li>duration: The duration of the animation in milliseconds.</li>\n<li>delay: The delay before the animation starts, in milliseconds.</li>\n</ul>\n","type":"AnimationModel","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#animation"},"bearFillColor":{"name":"bearFillColor","description":"<p>This property is used in financial charts to visualize price movements in stocks.\nIt defines the color of the candle/point when the opening price is less than the closing price.</p>\n","type":"string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#bearfillcolor"},"binInterval":{"name":"binInterval","description":"<p>The <code>binInterval</code> property controls the width of each bin and the interval between bins for histogram points.</p>\n","type":"number","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#bininterval"},"border":{"name":"border","description":"<p>Options for customizing the border of the series.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Note that this property is applicable only for <code>Column</code> and <code>Bar</code> type series.</p>\n</blockquote>\n","type":"BorderModel","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#border"},"boxPlotMode":{"name":"boxPlotMode","description":"<p>Specifies the box plot mode for the box and whisker chart series.\nThe available modes are:\nExclusive - Renders the series based on the exclusive mode.\nInclusive - Renders the series based on the inclusive mode.\nNormal - Renders the series based on the normal mode.</p>\n","type":"string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#boxplotmode"},"bullFillColor":{"name":"bullFillColor","description":"<p>This property is used in financial charts to visualize price movements in stocks.\nIt defines the color of the candle/point when the opening price is higher than the closing price.</p>\n","type":"string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#bullfillcolor"},"cardinalSplineTension":{"name":"cardinalSplineTension","description":"<p>Specifies the tension parameter for cardinal splines. This affects the curvature of the spline.</p>\n","type":"number","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#cardinalsplinetension"},"close":{"name":"close","description":"<p>The data source field that contains the close value.\nIt is applicable for both financial series and technical indicators.</p>\n","type":"string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#close"},"colorName":{"name":"colorName","description":"<p>The data source field that contains the color mapping value.\nIt is applicable for range color mapping.</p>\n","type":"string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#colorname"},"columnFacet":{"name":"columnFacet","description":"<p>Defines the shape of the data in a column and bar chart.\nAvailable shapes are:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Rectangle: Displays the data in a column and bar chart with a rectangular shape.</li>\n<li>Cylinder: Displays the data in a column and bar chart with a cylindrical shape.</li>\n</ul>\n","type":"string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#columnfacet"},"columnSpacing":{"name":"columnSpacing","description":"<p>This property determines the space between columns in a column or bar chart.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Note that it takes a value from 0 to 1.</p>\n</blockquote>\n","type":"number","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#columnspacing"},"columnWidth":{"name":"columnWidth","description":"<p>The <code>columnWidth</code> property can be used to customize the width of the columns in a column series.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Note that if the series type is histogram, the default value is 1; otherwise, it is 0.7.</p>\n</blockquote>\n","type":"number","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#columnwidth"},"columnWidthInPixel":{"name":"columnWidthInPixel","description":"<p>To render the column series points with a specific column width in pixels.</p>\n","type":"number","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#columnwidthinpixel"},"connector":{"name":"connector","description":"<p>Specifies the appearance of the line connecting adjacent points in waterfall charts.</p>\n","type":"ConnectorModel","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#connector"},"cornerRadius":{"name":"cornerRadius","description":"<p>The <code>cornerRadius</code> property specifies the radius for the corners of the column series points to create a rounded appearance in the chart.</p>\n","type":"CornerRadiusModel","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#cornerradius"},"dashArray":{"name":"dashArray","description":"<p>Defines the pattern of dashes and gaps used to stroke the lines in <code>Line</code> type series.</p>\n","type":"string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#dasharray"},"dataSource":{"name":"dataSource","description":"<p>Specifies the data source for the series. It can be an array of JSON objects, or an instance of DataManager.</p>\n","type":"Object|DataManager","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#datasource"},"dragSettings":{"name":"dragSettings","description":"<p>Customize the drag settings for the series with this property to configure drag behavior in the chart.</p>\n","type":"DragSettingsModel","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#dragsettings"},"drawType":{"name":"drawType","description":"<p>Specifies the type of series to be drawn in radar or polar charts.\nThe available options are:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>'Line' - Renders a line series.</li>\n<li>'Column' - Renders a column series.</li>\n<li>'Area' - Renders an area series.</li>\n<li>'Scatter' - Renders a scatter series.</li>\n<li>'Spline' - Renders a spline series.</li>\n<li>'StackingColumn' - Renders a stacking column series.</li>\n<li>'StackingArea' - Renders a stacking area series.</li>\n<li>'RangeColumn' - Renders a range column series.</li>\n<li>'SplineArea' - Renders a spline area series.</li>\n</ul>\n","type":"string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#drawtype"},"emptyPointSettings":{"name":"emptyPointSettings","description":"<p>Customization options for the appearance of empty points in the series.\n<code>null</code> or <code>undefined</code> values are considered empty points.</p>\n","type":"EmptyPointSettingsModel","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#emptypointsettings"},"enableComplexProperty":{"name":"enableComplexProperty","description":"<p>This property is used to improve chart performance through data mapping for the series data source.</p>\n","type":"boolean","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#enablecomplexproperty"},"enableSolidCandles":{"name":"enableSolidCandles","description":"<p>This property is applicable for the candle series.\nIt enables or disables the visual comparison of the current values with previous values in stock charts.</p>\n","type":"boolean","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#enablesolidcandles"},"enableTooltip":{"name":"enableTooltip","description":"<p>Controls whether the tooltip for the chart series is enabled or disabled. Set to true to display tooltips on hover, or false to hide them.</p>\n","type":"boolean","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#enabletooltip"},"errorBar":{"name":"errorBar","description":"<p>Options for displaying and customizing error bars for individual points in a series.</p>\n","type":"ErrorBarSettingsModel","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#errorbar"},"fill":{"name":"fill","description":"<p>The fill color for the series, which accepts values in hex or rgba as a valid CSS color string.\nIt also represents the color of the signal lines in technical indicators.\nFor technical indicators, the default value is 'blue', and for series, it is null.</p>\n","type":"string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#fill"},"groupName":{"name":"groupName","description":"<p>Defines the name that specifies the chart series are mutually exclusive and can be overlaid.\nSeries in the same group share the same baseline and location on the corresponding axis.</p>\n","type":"string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#groupname"},"high":{"name":"high","description":"<p>The data source field that contains the high value.\nIt is applicable for both financial series and technical indicators.</p>\n","type":"string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#high"},"intermediateSumIndexes":{"name":"intermediateSumIndexes","description":"<p>Defines the collection of indexes for the intermediate summary columns in waterfall charts.</p>\n","type":"number[]","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#intermediatesumindexes"},"isClosed":{"name":"isClosed","description":"<p>Specifies whether to join the start and end points of a line/area series used in a polar/radar chart to form a closed path.</p>\n","type":"boolean","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#isclosed"},"labelSettings":{"name":"labelSettings","description":"<p>Configures the options for displaying series names as inline labels in the chart.</p>\n","type":"SeriesLabelSettingsModel","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#labelsettings"},"lastValueLabel":{"name":"lastValueLabel","description":"<p>Options for customizing and displaying the last value in the series.</p>\n","type":"LastValueLabelSettingsModel","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#lastvaluelabel"},"legendImageUrl":{"name":"legendImageUrl","description":"<p>The URL for the image to be displayed as a legend icon.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Note that <code>legendShape</code> must be set to <code>Image</code>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n","type":"string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#legendimageurl"},"legendShape":{"name":"legendShape","description":"<p>Specifies the shape of the legend icon for each series.\nAvailable shapes for legend:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Circle - Renders a circular icon.</li>\n<li>Rectangle - Renders a rectangular icon.</li>\n<li>Triangle - Renders a triangular icon.</li>\n<li>Diamond - Renders a diamond-shaped icon.</li>\n<li>Cross - Renders a cross-shaped icon.</li>\n<li>HorizontalLine - Renders a horizontal line icon.</li>\n<li>VerticalLine - Renders a vertical line icon.</li>\n<li>Pentagon - Renders a pentagon-shaped icon.</li>\n<li>InvertedTriangle - Renders an inverted triangle-shaped icon.</li>\n<li>SeriesType - Uses the default icon shape based on the series type.</li>\n<li>Image - Renders a custom image for the legend icon.</li>\n</ul>\n","type":"string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#legendshape"},"linearGradient":{"name":"linearGradient","description":"<p>Applies a linear gradient fill to the series.\nThe gradient transitions colors along a straight line.\nWhen both linearGradient and radialGradient are specified, linearGradient takes precedence.</p>\n","type":"LinearGradientModel","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#lineargradient"},"low":{"name":"low","description":"<p>The data source field that contains the low value.\nIt is applicable for both financial series and technical indicators.</p>\n","type":"string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#low"},"marker":{"name":"marker","description":"<p>Options for displaying and customizing markers for individual points in a series.</p>\n","type":"MarkerSettingsModel","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#marker"},"maxRadius":{"name":"maxRadius","description":"<p>Specifies the maximum radius for the data points in the series.</p>\n","type":"number","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#maxradius"},"minRadius":{"name":"minRadius","description":"<p>Specifies the minimum radius for the data points in the series.</p>\n","type":"number","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#minradius"},"name":{"name":"name","description":"<p>The <code>name</code> property allows setting a name for the series, which will be displayed in the legend, identifying different series in the chart, especially when multiple series are present.</p>\n","type":"string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#name"},"negativeFillColor":{"name":"negativeFillColor","description":"<p>Defines the visual representation of negative changes in waterfall charts.</p>\n","type":"string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#negativefillcolor"},"noRisers":{"name":"noRisers","description":"<p>When set to true, the step series will be rendered without the vertical lines (risers) connecting the horizontal steps.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Note this property is only applicable to step series.</p>\n</blockquote>\n","type":"boolean","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#norisers"},"nonHighlightStyle":{"name":"nonHighlightStyle","description":"<p>The <code>nonHighlightStyle</code> property is used to specify custom CSS styles for the non-highlighted series or points.</p>\n","type":"string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#nonhighlightstyle"},"opacity":{"name":"opacity","description":"<p>Sets the opacity of the series, with a value between 0 and 1 where 0 is fully transparent and 1 is fully opaque.</p>\n","type":"number","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#opacity"},"open":{"name":"open","description":"<p>The data source field that contains the open value.\nIt is applicable for both financial series and technical indicators.</p>\n","type":"string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#open"},"paretoOptions":{"name":"paretoOptions","description":"<p>Options for customizing the Pareto line series, including its appearance and behavior in the chart.</p>\n","type":"ParetoOptionsModel","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#paretooptions"},"pointColorMapping":{"name":"pointColorMapping","description":"<p>The data source field that contains the color value of a point.\nIt is applicable for series.</p>\n","type":"string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#pointcolormapping"},"query":{"name":"query","description":"<p>Specifies a query to select data from the data source. This property is applicable only when the data source is an <code>ej.DataManager</code>.</p>\n","type":"Query","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#query"},"radialGradient":{"name":"radialGradient","description":"<p>Applies a radial gradient fill to the series.\nThe gradient transitions colors outward from a central point.</p>\n","type":"RadialGradientModel","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#radialgradient"},"rangeColorPoints":{"name":"rangeColorPoints","description":"","type":"string[]","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#rangecolorpoints"},"removedPointIndex":{"name":"removedPointIndex","description":"","type":"number","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#removedpointindex"},"segmentAxis":{"name":"segmentAxis","description":"<p>Defines the axis along which the line series will be split.</p>\n","type":"string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#segmentaxis"},"segments":{"name":"segments","description":"<p>Specifies a collection of regions used to differentiate a line series.</p>\n","type":"ChartSegmentModel[]","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#segments"},"selectionStyle":{"name":"selectionStyle","description":"<p>The <code>selectionStyle</code> property is used to specify custom CSS styles for the selected series or points.</p>\n","type":"string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#selectionstyle"},"showMean":{"name":"showMean","description":"<p>If set to true, the mean value for the box and whisker plot will be visible.</p>\n","type":"boolean","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#showmean"},"showNearestTooltip":{"name":"showNearestTooltip","description":"<p>Enables or disables the display of tooltips for the nearest data point to the cursor for series.</p>\n","type":"boolean","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#shownearesttooltip"},"showNormalDistribution":{"name":"showNormalDistribution","description":"<p>Specifies whether to display the normal distribution curve for the histogram series.</p>\n","type":"boolean","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#shownormaldistribution"},"showOutliers":{"name":"showOutliers","description":"<p>Specifies whether to display outliers in the Box and Whisker chart.\nIf set to <code>true</code>, outliers will be displayed as individual points beyond the whiskers, representing data points that significantly differ from the rest of the dataset.\nIf set to <code>false</code>, outliers will be hidden, and only the box, median, and whiskers will be rendered.</p>\n<p>Outliers are typically used to identify extreme values in statistical data representation.</p>\n","type":"boolean","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#showoutliers"},"size":{"name":"size","description":"<p>The data source field that contains the size value for the y-axis.</p>\n","type":"string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#size"},"splineType":{"name":"splineType","description":"<p>Specifies the type of spline used for rendering.\nAvailable options include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Natural - Renders a natural spline.</li>\n<li>Cardinal - Renders a cardinal spline.</li>\n<li>Clamped - Renders a clamped spline.</li>\n<li>Monotonic - Renders a monotonic spline.</li>\n</ul>\n","type":"string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#splinetype"},"stackingGroup":{"name":"stackingGroup","description":"<p>This property allows the grouping of series in stacked column and stacked bar charts.\nAny string value can be assigned to the <code>stackingGroup</code> property.\nSeries with the same <code>stackingGroup</code> value will be grouped together in the chart.</p>\n","type":"string","link":"//ej2.syncfusion.com/javascript/documentation/api/chart/series#stackinggroup"},"step":{"name":"step","description":"<p>The <code>step</code> property can be used to change the position of the steps in step line, step area, and step range area chart types.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Left: Steps start from the left side of the 2nd point.</li>\n